SERVER v5.89 — "THE SERVICING TRACKER READS ITS OWN TICKS BACK". Written as `patch_server_v589.py` in the v5.87 style: a base SHA guard of d5a0d777da4871af1bf88804b4ef223354a29c2560213ab56f7897445b398fdc, and a local rep() where each replacement must match exactly once (patch_server_v587.py lines 20-32). Every anchor below was applied cleanly in the prototype. The shipped version carries Andrew's words in the comments (18 Oct: "purely just a track", "its own separate html that is linked to nothing else. But still links results to main", "Then tick when complete. Each section will automatically update. With a percentage of completion. Log the time the reference was done").

1. FILES (line 69): after `scoped:` add
   `ticks: path.join(DATA_DIR, 'tracker_ticks.json'),   /* v5.89 — the servicing tracker's ticks, a store of their own */`

2. NEW BLOCK after pruneReports (lines 220-228). The comment says a tick is somebody's word in its own store. It never touches the record, a delivery, a light, a charge, the card reports or their pruning. Nothing here reads the record. The server stores and works nothing out.
```js
const MAX_TICK_BODY = 2 * 1024, MAX_TICKS_PER_CARD = 5000, MAX_TICKS_TOTAL = 20000;
const TICK_ROW_RE = /^[A-Za-z0-9?_.-]{1,16}$/, TICK_ID_RE = /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,40}$/, TICK_DAY_RE = /^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/;
function ticksShape(v) { return plainObject(v) && Object.values(v).every(t => plainObject(t) && Number.isInteger(t.seq) && Array.isArray(t.list)); }
let ticks = loadStore(FILES.ticks, 'tracker ticks', 'ticks', ticksShape) || {};   // snapshot fallback (step 3), so a damaged file recovers instead of stopping the service
function persistTicks() { try { writeWhole(FILES.ticks, ticks); return null; } catch (e) { console.error('ticks', e.message); return e; } }
function ticksFor(token) { return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(ticks, token) ? ticks[token] : null; }
function ticksTotal() { return Object.values(ticks).reduce((n, t) => n + t.list.length, 0); }
function trackerConfig(t) {   // the editor's own list: rows are locations, days are service days; both or nothing
  if (!plainObject(t)) return null;
  const rows = [...new Set((Array.isArray(t.rows) ? t.rows : []).map(r => String(r).trim()))].filter(r => TICK_ROW_RE.test(r) && !protoKey(r)).slice(0, 400);
  const days = [...new Set((Array.isArray(t.days) ? t.days : []).map(d => String(d)))].filter(d => TICK_DAY_RE.test(d)).sort().slice(0, 7);
  return rows.length && days.length ? { rows, days } : null;
}
function tickOut(x, withName) {   // the typed name only behind the edit link
  const o = { id: x.id, seq: x.seq, row: x.row, day: x.day, done: x.done, at: x.at, tapped_at: x.tapped_at };
  if (withName) o.name_given = x.name_given;
  return o;
}
```
   TICK_ROW_RE is separate from REF_RE (line 803) because REF_RE drops the 'Spare' row (0164) in areas13.json.

3. snapshot() (line 603): add `['ticks', ticks, FILES.ticks]` to the list. This gives hourly and boot snapshots, which loadStore can recover from. The existing per-prefix rotation applies, and v5.87 ignores ticks-* files.

4. POST /api/cards: after the cards[token] object is built, before `pruneCards();` (line 2809):
